<title>ROMANIA: Romania suspends Bulgaria livestock imports-agency.</title>
<headline>Romania suspends Bulgaria livestock imports-agency.</headline>
<dateline>BUCHAREST 1996-11-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Romania has temporarily banned livestock imports from neighbouring Bulgaria following an outbreak there of foot-and-mouth disease, the independent Mediafax news agency said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Mediafax quoted a farm ministry statement as saying the state-run National Sanitary Veterinary Association (ANSV) had taken steps to stop the disease spreading into Romania.</p>
<p>Bulgaria, which last had an outbreak of the disease in 1993, earlier this year banned imports of meat and dairy products from Greece, Turkey, rump Yugoslavia and Macedonia and withdrew herds from border areas.</p>
<p>Agriculture Ministry officials were not available for comment.</p>
<p>--Bucharest Newsroom +40-1 3120264</p>
